From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:30:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A session switch re-runs only the two rail rows whose
 selection changes, since each row asks a selector over the shown session
 instead of comparing the shown id itself, and the session list's order keeps
 its identity until a row joins, leaves or moves, so the first read's row no
 longer regroups every project's rows in the task that paints the destination,
 and a first visit's seen mark neither regroups them nor rebuilds every
 mounted timeline's session rows; the app's line budget is the measured
 107,819.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
